<!--
Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel J. Mazure
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause (as the OpenPiton devices.xml it extends)

Peripheral address map for OpenPiton + Microwatt on the AMD Kria KV260
(KV260_BOARD -> PITONSYS_SHELL). There is no board DDR for the manycore:
memory is a 512 MB carve-out of the ZynqMP PS DDR, reached through the
chipset's AXI4 master and rr-openpiton's pmesh_hp_shim (PS = 0x4000_0000 +
PA). mem.length MUST equal the shim's WINDOW and mc_define.h
BOARD_MEM_SIZE_MB; anything beyond it is answered DECERR by the shim.

The UART is the chipset 16550; on the board its TX/RX are cross-connected in
fabric to PS UART0 over EMIO (null modem), so PS Linux reads the manycore
console on /dev/ttyPS0.

mw_xics is Microwatt's XICS (ICP at +0, ICS at +0x1000) as a chipset device
(rr-openpiton hw/ip/mw_xics, OPN-P2.15). It must be paired with the
PITON_MW_XICS define, which carries its interrupt wires to the tiles;
chipset_impl refuses to elaborate if the two disagree. It is a pure slave, so
no noc2in. A port listed here must have a chipset device behind it.

mw_syscon is Microwatt's syscon (rr-openpiton hw/ip/mw_syscon, OPN-P2.24) at
core 0xC000_0000, where Linux's Microwatt SMP code looks for CPU_CTRL. It must
be paired with PITON_MW_SYSCON, which carries its run wires to the tiles.
-->
<devices>
    <!--The first entry should always be the filter/chip to xbar connection-->
    <port>
        <name>chip</name>
        <noc2in/>
    </port>
    <port>
        <name>mem</name>
        <base>0x0</base>
        <!-- 512 MB PS-DDR carve-out -->
        <length>0x20000000</length>
    </port>
    <port>
        <name>iob</name>
        <base>0x9f00000000</base>
        <length>0x10</length>
        <noc2in/>
    </port>
    <port>
        <name>uart</name>
        <base>0xfff0c2c000</base>
        <length>0xd4000</length>
        <noc2in/>
    </port>
    <port>
        <name>mw_syscon</name>
        <!-- core address 0xC000_0000: Linux microwatt smp.c SYSCON_BASE / SYSCON_LENGTH -->
        <base>0xfff0000000</base>
        <length>0x100</length>
    </port>
    <port>
        <name>mw_xics</name>
        <!-- core address 0xC0D0_0000 (mw_piton_core.v 0xC... window) -->
        <base>0xfff0d00000</base>
        <length>0x2000</length>
    </port>
</devices>
